 seconds at the US Trials. In the final, Echevarría set a suicidal pace on the first 100, leading Burton, and he paid the price by 200 metres, already falling back. Burton was steady, leading by three lengths at 500 metres, Echevarría holding on for second. By 1,000 metres America’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/51446"} "John Kinsella"] " had moved into second, but he was 18 metres in back of Burton, who had the race in hand, and Echevarría had dropped to near the back of the pack. Burton eventually won by 18.4 seconds over Kinsella, with Australia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/45164"} "Greg Brough"] " taking the bronze medal, while Echevarría finished sixth. In 1972 at Munich, Burton would return and defend his gold medal. In August 1970, Kinsella became the first swimmer to break 16 minutes for the 1,500. He later became a professional open water swimmer, winning many events, and is one of the few Olympic swimmers to have successfully crossed the English Channel."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "15345"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51283"} "Mike Burton"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "17:27.2 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "16:38.9 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "15355"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51446"} "John Kinsella"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "17:22.7 (2 h3)"] [:td {} "16:57.3 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [